0. THE PRODUCT INTENTION (applies to every screen in every phase)

This is the guiding principle. Cursor: hold this above all styling decisions.

Plain language on the surface. Full clinical accuracy underneath.

The user is never shown jargon without a plain explanation right next to it.
Every test, finding, and recommendation gets a one-line "what it is / what it does" in everyday words.
BUT the exact clinical term from the source document is always kept too — shown as a secondary label, tooltip, or "medical name" line. We never omit or dumb down the real specification; we translate it.
The dashboard and navigation must be simple enough for someone who has never used a health app. One clear action per screen. No dead ends. No confusing menus.

Concrete pattern to use everywhere a clinical term appears:

Gut health check                      ← plain name (big, primary)
Looks at how your gut bacteria and    ← one-line plain explanation
digestion may affect hormone balance
Medical name: Stool beta-glucuronidase & microbial diversity   ← exact term kept, smaller/secondary

Build a reusable <ClinicalTerm> component that takes plainName, plainExplanation, and medicalName, and renders exactly this pattern. Use it every single time a Tier test, gene, or finding is displayed. This one component is how we keep the promise: simple on top, accurate underneath.

1. WHAT PHASE 2 ADDS (scope)

Phase 1 ended at: user completes questionnaire → rules engine recommends tests → a simple list. Phase 2 makes it a real closed loop:

IN scope for Phase 2:

Lab results storage & upload — a way for results to enter the app (manual entry / clinician upload / CSV — no live lab API yet).
Results dashboard — plain-language display of what each result means, with the exact clinical marker kept underneath.
The full rules engine, activated — now that lab data can exist, the Tier 4 triggers and the results→intervention map from the document actually fire.
Personalised plan screen — the intervention list generated from results, every item in plain language + exact clinical basis, clearly marked "pending practitioner review."
Follow-up & re-test tracking — reminders, and the recurring symptom re-check from the document.
First Edge Function — one server-side function for anything that must not run on the phone (e.g. writing clinician-reviewed results securely). Introduced gently, with full explanation.

STILL OUT of scope (save for Phase 3): AI coaching chat, supplement e-commerce/payments, live lab-ordering APIs, B2B/practitioner portal, push-notification infrastructure beyond simple local reminders.

2. NEW SUPABASE TABLES (paste into SQL Editor — NOT the Edge Functions editor)

Reminder for the non-coder: SQL goes in Dashboard → SQL Editor. TypeScript (anything starting with import or Deno.serve) goes in Dashboard → Edge Functions. Never mix them — pasting a function into the SQL box is the syntax error at or near "import" error.

sql
-- ========== TEST RESULTS ==========
CREATE TABLE public.test_results (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  user_id UUID REFERENCES public.profiles(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  test_order_id UUID REFERENCES public.test_orders(id),
  test_name TEXT NOT NULL,          -- exact clinical marker name
  plain_name TEXT,                  -- everyday name shown to user
  result_value TEXT,
  result_unit TEXT,
  reference_range TEXT,
  flag TEXT CHECK (flag IN ('normal','low','high','critical','positive','negative')),
  lab_report_url TEXT,              -- optional PDF in Supabase Storage
  clinician_reviewed BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE,
  reviewed_by TEXT,
  reviewed_at TIMESTAMPTZ,
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()
);
ALTER TABLE public.test_results ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
CREATE POLICY "own_results" ON public.test_results
  FOR ALL USING (auth.uid() = user_id) WITH CHECK (auth.uid() = user_id);

-- ========== INTERVENTIONS (the personalised plan) ==========
CREATE TABLE public.interventions (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  user_id UUID REFERENCES public.profiles(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  trigger_finding TEXT NOT NULL,    -- which result/answer triggered this (exact term)
  plain_reason TEXT,                -- plain-language "why you're seeing this"
  category TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (category IN (
    'supplement','diet','lifestyle','therapy','referral','coaching'
  )),
  title TEXT NOT NULL,              -- plain-language action title
  description TEXT,
  clinical_basis TEXT,              -- exact intervention text from the protocol
  status TEXT DEFAULT 'draft' CHECK (status IN (
    'draft','clinician_approved','active','paused','completed','declined'
  )),
  approved_by TEXT,
  approved_at TIMESTAMPTZ,
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()
);
ALTER TABLE public.interventions ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
CREATE POLICY "own_interventions" ON public.interventions
  FOR ALL USING (auth.uid() = user_id) WITH CHECK (auth.uid() = user_id);

-- ========== FOLLOW-UPS ==========
CREATE TABLE public.follow_ups (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  user_id UUID REFERENCES public.profiles(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  type TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (type IN ('retest','review','symptom_check','coaching')),
  title TEXT NOT NULL,
  plain_note TEXT,
  due_date DATE NOT NULL,
  status TEXT DEFAULT 'pending' CHECK (status IN ('pending','completed','missed','rescheduled')),
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()
);
ALTER TABLE public.follow_ups ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
CREATE POLICY "own_followups" ON public.follow_ups
  FOR ALL USING (auth.uid() = user_id) WITH CHECK (auth.uid() = user_id);

