Safety cross-checks that must run before any intervention is shown (from the doc's guardrails):

Iodine intervention is hard-blocked if thyroid antibodies positive — reuse the Phase 1 hard-stop.
Before showing DIM/I3C or high-dose omega-3, flag a clinician_interaction_check if the user reported hormone therapy or blood thinners (questionnaire) — the app shows the item as "needs practitioner check" rather than a plain go-ahead.
Every intervention row is created with status: 'draft' and displays a persistent "pending practitioner review" banner. The app never presents an intervention as an instruction.

