6. FIRST EDGE FUNCTION (gentle intro for the non-coder)

Phase 2 needs one server-side function: writing clinician-reviewed results so they can't be forged on the phone. Here's exactly what to do — this is TypeScript, it goes in Edge Functions, not the SQL editor.

Cursor: scaffold with the CLI, use the current Deno.serve + jsr:@supabase/supabase-js@2 pattern (this is the current stable pattern as of 2026), and explain each step to me in plain English.

ts
// supabase/functions/save-reviewed-result/index.ts
import { createClient } from "jsr:@supabase/supabase-js@2";

Deno.serve(async (req) => {
  try {
    const { record } = await req.json();

    // Service-role client stays server-side ONLY — never in the app.
    const supabase = createClient(
      Deno.env.get("SUPABASE_URL")!,
      Deno.env.get("SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY")!
    );

    // Basic validation so bad data can't land in the table.
    if (!record?.user_id || !record?.test_name) {
      return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: "Missing required fields" }), {
        status: 400, headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
      });
    }

    const { data, error } = await supabase
      .from("test_results")
      .insert({ ...record, clinician_reviewed: true, reviewed_at: new Date().toISOString() })
      .select()
      .single();

    if (error) throw error;

    return new Response(JSON.stringify({ data }), {
      status: 200, headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
    });
  } catch (e) {
    return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: String(e) }), {
      status: 500, headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
    });
  }
});

Deploy: supabase functions deploy save-reviewed-result. Set the secret once: supabase secrets set SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=... (find it in Dashboard → Settings → API). The service-role key NEVER goes in the app — only here, server-side. This is the one rule that keeps results trustworthy.

